        "label:n1->n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For the Part Provision Team, the first step is to identify the parts."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly starts the process (init), defines the first concrete step (action), and the connection label redundantly restates the same instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "label:n2->n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the team needs to elicit information from the customer, they should then check the availability of the parts."
      ],
      "justification": "The action and label capture the conditional inquiry; the branch node captures the logical split implied by the conditional."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "check the availability of the parts"
      ],
      "justification": "Direct, exact match to the required availability check action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if they need to record the customer's details, they should order and receive the part from Disuki."
      ],
      "justification": "Action captures the condition; branch splits the path; guard routes to the ordering sequence; actions n6 and n7 correctly decompose the compound 'order and receive' instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the parts are supplied to the customer, the team can also continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard captures the supply condition; action represents the resulting supplied state."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the part is received, the team can then contract the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the contracting action that follows part receipt."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10",
        "label:n10->n11",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After all the necessary parts are collected, the team can proceed with the payment."
      ],
      "justification": "Convergence rejoins split paths before collection; actions and label sequentially match the collection and payment steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:n11->n12",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the payment is made, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Label denotes payment completion; action and structural end node correctly terminate the process."
    }
